{"name":"Josephine","hex":"#d3c3be","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Josephine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from French."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to Joseph II, Holy Roman Emperor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Josephine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Josephine (given name)","blocks":[{"text":"Josephine is a female name. It is the English version of the French name Joséphine, itself a female variant of the name Joseph, which is ultimately derived from the Hebrew name Yosef, meaning \"he shall add/grow\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josephine_(given_name)","wikidata":"Q666954"},{"title":"Josephine (singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Jessica Josephine Wendel, known professionally as Josephine, is a Greek singer. She is known for her participation in the Greek national final for the Eurovision Song Contest 2014 with the song \"Dancing Night\". Wendel has also competed in the Greek edition of the Your Face Sounds Familiar. On 26 December 2020, she won the fourth Greek season of Just the 2 of Us, along with actor and entrepreneur Nasos Papargyropoulos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Josephine_%282019%29_%28cropped%29.png/330px-Josephine_%282019%29_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josephine_(singer)","wikidata":"Q48022109"},{"title":"Josephine (2026 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Josephine is a 2026 American thriller-drama film, written, directed, and produced by Beth de Araújo. It stars Channing Tatum, Gemma Chan, Mason Reeves, Philip Ettinger, and Syra McCarthy."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Josephine_(2026_film)","wikidata":"Q128502486"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"Josephine":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6d/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-Josephine.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_ca